---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description={`About ${SITE.name} — background, experience, and what I'm looking for.`}
>
  <div class="wrap about">
    <h1>About</h1>

    <!-- This is drafted from your CV summary. Read it aloud once and adjust
         anything that doesn't sound like you — it should read as a person
         talking, not a profile being recited. -->
    <p>
      I'm a data and AI engineer based in Khmelnytskyi, Ukraine. For the past
      eight years I've worked on the systems that sit between raw data and the
      decisions people make with it — pipelines, warehouses, and more recently
      the LLM applications that read from them.
    </p>

    <p>
      Most of my work lately has been production RAG systems and AI agents:
      retrieval that returns the right context, agents that behave predictably
      enough to ship, and the evaluation and observability needed to trust either
      one. That's built on LangChain, LangGraph, the OpenAI Agent SDK, and vector
      search, but the hard part is rarely the framework — it's the retrieval
      quality and the data feeding it.
    </p>

    <p>
      Underneath that is the part I've done longest: ETL and ELT pipelines,
      analytical warehouses, real-time streaming, and distributed platforms in
      Python, Spark, Databricks, Kafka, dbt, Airflow, Dagster, and AWS. I've built
      recommendation engines, personalization, and reverse ETL across fintech,
      healthcare, e-commerce, marketing, and iGaming. I care about the unglamorous
      properties — data quality, governance, and observability — because they're
      what decide whether a system survives contact with production.
    </p>

    <p>
      <!-- TODO: Make this specific. What role do you actually want next, and
           are you open to remote / relocation? This is the sentence that turns
           a reader into an email. -->
      I'm currently looking for [the kind of role you want]. If you're working on
      something in this space, I'd like to hear about it.
    </p>

    <h2>Experience</h2>
    <!-- TODO: Replace with your real roles. Keep it brief — the CV carries the
         detail, and duplicating it here just creates two things to keep in sync. -->
    <ul class="roles">
      <li>
        <span class="role-title">Senior Data &amp; AI Engineer</span>
        <span class="org">Company</span>
        <span class="dates">20XX — Present</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="role-title">Previous Title</span>
        <span class="org">Earlier Company</span>
        <span class="dates">20XX — 20XX</span>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="cv-note">
      <!-- Put your CV PDF in public/ and it'll be served at this path. -->
      Full history: <a href="/cv.pdf">download CV (PDF)</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
    <p>
      Reach me at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about {
    padding-top: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .about h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-md);
  }

  .roles {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-md);
  }

  .roles li {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.1rem;
    padding-bottom: var(--space-md);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .roles li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .role-title {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .org,
  .dates {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }

  .dates {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
  }

  .cv-note {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
</style>
